WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en
NOTE Emergency Response Flood Rescue Operations - WebVTT Caption File
NOTE Authored for ResQNet CSC413-8 Lab Exercise 2
NOTE Timestamps are illustrative, authored for a 90-second disaster-response training clip.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
<c.emergency-cue>ALERT: Cyclone Vardha flooding has breached the embankment at Sector 4.</c>

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.200
<c.location-cue>Location: Krishna Basin, Grid Reference 16.5125° N, 80.6420° E.</c>

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Emergency teams from the National Disaster Response Force are deploying
swift water rescue units along the eastern flood corridor.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.800
<c.action-cue>NDRF personnel prepare inflatable rescue boats</c>
at the staging area near Highway 12 Junction.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.500
Approximately 165 civilians are confirmed stranded on rooftops
in the Sector 4 and St. Jude Basin residential zones.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.200
<c.emergency-cue>CRITICAL: Bridge collapse reported on River Road near Sector 4.</c>
All surface approach routes are severed.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:39.000
<c.action-cue>Helicopter evacuation request authorised</c>
for elderly and medical-priority civilians at Grid Point Alpha-7.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.500
Coast Guard marine patrol units are en route via waterway,
estimated arrival at the flood zone in 12 minutes.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:52.000
Field teams are reporting a critical shortage of potable drinking water
at the Sunrise School evacuation shelter — currently 340 occupants.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:58.500
<c.location-cue>Field Hospital Alpha is operational at St. Thomas Church, Sector 2.</c>
Medical triage capacity: 85 beds, 6 ICU units.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:05.000
ResQNet field coordination software is running in offline-first mode.
<c.action-cue>All incident records are stored locally in browser IndexedDB.</c>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:11.500
Synchronisation queue contains 7 pending reports
awaiting upload when network connectivity is restored.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:18.200
<c.action-cue>Red Cross Mobile ICU is now on scene</c>
at the Sector 4 rooftop rescue point. Medical assessment underway.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:24.000
Evacuation Corridor Echo — the northern road through Highway 12 bypass —
is confirmed clear for outbound civilian movement.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:30.500
<c.emergency-cue>All rescue teams: maintain radio contact on VHF Channel 16.</c>
Incident Commander is located at EOC Central HQ.

NOTE End of captions for emergency-response.mp4
NOTE Total duration: approximately 90 seconds

